# The Cholesky workload with K written out as a literal, which the checker can
# prove positive definite (up to 32 x 32), so `K⁻¹ @ f` is a Cholesky solve on
# every engine. Same K as the other languages build: c1 c1ᵀ + c2 c2ᵀ + n I.
K: PositiveDefinite Matrix[{{N}}, {{N}}] = {{KMAT:N}}
f = {{VEC:2:N}}
ones = {{VEC:ones:N}}
acc = 0.0
x = f
for r in range({{R}}):
    x = K⁻¹ @ ((1 + r) * f)
    acc = acc + x[0] + x[{{N}} - 1] + ones @ x
print(acc, x[0], x[{{N}} - 1])
